$ yo compile --help
Usage: yo compile <file.yo> [options]

Compile a '.yo' source file to a native executable (via C11).

Options:
  -o <path>                 Output binary path
  --optimize <level>        C optimization level (0|1|2|3); default is -O0.
                            Use 2 for real builds. Any level above 0 also
                            enables the ThinLTO pairing that --emit-chunks
                            requires.
  -g, --debug-symbols       Emit debug symbols
  -s, --strip               Strip the output binary
  --cc, --c-compiler <cc>   C compiler to use (clang|gcc|zig|emcc)
  -t, --target <triple>     Cross-compile target (e.g. <TARGET>, wasm32-wasip1)
  --sysroot <dir>           Sysroot for cross-compilation
  --cflags '<flags>'        Extra flags passed to the C compiler
  -D, --define <N[=V]>      Preprocessor define for the C compile
  -I <dir> / -L <dir>       Include / library search path
  -l <name>                 Link a library
  --extern <spec>           Extern library spec (pkg-config integration)
  --static                  Static link
  --static-library          Build a static library instead of an executable
  --shared-library          Build a shared library (lib<name>.dylib/.so/.dll)
  --sanitize <kind>         Sanitizer (address|thread|undefined)
  --disable-sanitize        Drop sanitizer flags added by defaults
  --allocator <name>        Allocator (system|mimalloc|fixed)
  --heap-size <size>        Fixed-region heap, e.g. 16M (only with --allocator fixed; 64K..4G)
  --debug-heap              Print heap stats + live-at-exit leak oracle at exit (fixed only)
  --emit-c                  Print the generated C to stdout and stop
  --emit-c-to <path>        Write the generated C to a file and stop
  --emit-deps <path>        Write the files this compile read, one per line
  --skip-c-compiler         Generate C but skip the C compile
  --skip-codegen            Evaluate only (no C generation)
  --emit-chunks <n|auto>    Split emitted C into n translation units (implies -flto=thin);
                            auto picks n from emitted size and core count (YO_JOBS overrides)
  --no-chunk-lto            Opt out of ThinLTO for chunked builds
  --jobs <n>                Parallel C compiles for chunked builds
  --compile-timeout-ms <ms> C compiler timeout
  --profile                 Print per-phase / per-module timing on stderr
  --profile-json <path>     Write the profile as JSON (module keys are absolute paths)
  --emcc-environment <env>  Emscripten environment (node|web)
  --debug-gc / --debug-async-await / --debug-parallelism
                            Runtime debug logging in the emitted binary
  --std-path <dir>          Override the std library directory

Examples:
  $ yo compile main.yo -o app
  $ yo compile main.yo --optimize 2 --target <TARGET> -o app
  $ yo compile main.yo --emit-c --skip-c-compiler --optimize 2
